  "slug": "rna-fragment-d584",
  "summary": "Arabidopsis cross-linking MS now provides proteome-scale residue contacts, while new workflows tie PTMs and variants to those structural networks.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is residue-resolved structural information used to connect molecular features to protein function. The PhoX cross-linking MS resource for Arabidopsis reports 37,531 residue-level contacts across 5,064 proteins, defining 3,083 protein-protein interactions, giving measured proteome-scale interaction architecture. Scop3P-Toolkit, a preprint, links PTMs, peptides, and variants to structural and residue interaction networks through open-source, notebook- and Galaxy-based workflows. What is new is the pairing of proteome-scale residue-level interaction maps with reproducible analysis frameworks that tie modifications and variants to structure. ChlORIS, also a preprint, contributes a different layer, providing 496 consistent plastid orthogroups from 2,254 algal plastid genomes with calibrated HMMs, alignments, and predicted structures. The items are heterogeneous, and the genomic resource does not itself report interaction measurements.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-08-15"
}
